**The drawing:** the tip is at the top-left corner and the handle at the bottom-right. The blade has a straight spine, a heel line, and one curve for the cutting edge. That curve starts parallel to the spine at the heel and bends up steeply near the tip. The handle is a hollow rounded bar flush with the spine and set back from the bottom of the blade at the heel. The blade is about 2.2 times as long as it is deep and about 1.5 times as deep as the handle, close to the generated PNG. I checked it at 48 px on light and dark backgrounds and it reads clearly as a kitchen knife. I tried four versions: the first looked like a cleaver and the second like a spade. Of the last two I kept the one with the rounder curve near the tip.

